      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Wealth taxes show mixed results globally: while some European nations adopted them to fund public services without burdening the working class, the U.S. and UK rejected them, arguing they stall capital formation. A 2017 Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development study found that many wealth tax revenues were eventually reallocated to services that offset higher prices for poorer households. Ultimately, its effectiveness depends on robust enforcement and whether the resulting public spending actively supports economic growth rather than just increasing the cost of living.",
